                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Zzzz-Zzzz-Zzzz is a really strange little adventure game, and I liked how different it feels from a normal platformer. The whole game is built around dreams, with the goal being to somehow wake up from a constantly changing collection of surreal worlds. I enjoyed the uncertainty because I never completely knew what kind of place I was going to enter next.\n\nThe platforming itself is fairly simple, but the game is more interested in exploration and puzzle solving than pure precision. I move through dream environments, look for ways forward and try to understand what each strange area is asking me to do. I liked that the challenge is often about figuring out where to go rather than simply making difficult jumps.\n\nThe non linear structure is probably my favorite part. I am not always pushed through the same obvious route, and some areas feel more like places I have to understand than levels I simply have to complete. That makes the experience feel like a dream where logic is present, but never completely reliable.\n\nThe dream settings are also full of variety. Some areas are peaceful and almost beautiful, while others contain zombies, dangerous obstacles and strange reflections. I liked the contrast because it keeps the atmosphere unpredictable. One moment I can be walking through clouds and the next I am dealing with something much more unsettling.\n\nThe presentation has a very old school pixel art feel that suits the dream theme. The music also helps give some of the calmer sections a strange sense of comfort before the game suddenly changes direction. I especially liked how the environments are allowed to feel mysterious instead of explaining every detail immediately.\n\nMy biggest issue is that the abstract structure can sometimes become confusing. There were moments when I understood that I was supposed to find something but had no clear idea where to look. That can be interesting when I am in the right mood, but it can also turn into aimless wandering. The game expects me to experiment and pay attention more than it expects me to follow instructions.\n\nOverall, Zzzz-Zzzz-Zzzz is a weird and memorable dream adventure that I found surprisingly enjoyable. I liked the surreal worlds, the non linear structure and the mixture of platforming with environmental puzzles. It can definitely be confusing at times, but that strange dream logic is also a big part of what makes the game stand out.\n\nRating: 6.8/10\n",
